<!-- The IMF's World Economic Outlook dataflow with its data structure, written by hand from the SDMX 2.1 standard
     (the IMF could not be reached when it was made, so this is not the IMF's own answer). It holds each way SDMX 2.1
     gives a dimension's codes that the browser must follow:
     COUNTRY    its own representation names IMF:CL_WEO_COUNTRY(1.0), but the answer has that list only as
                IMF.RES:CL_WEO_COUNTRY(2.0) (a code list kept by another agency); a constraint narrows it.
     INDICATOR  no representation of its own: its concept (given by URN) is represented by IMF.RES:CL_WEO_INDICATOR,
                with names and descriptions; another scheme's concept of the same id points elsewhere, and a
                constraint's excluded region drops NGAP_NPGDP.
     FREQUENCY  a URN to SDMX:CL_FREQ(2.1), not in the answer: asked for on its own (sdmx_cl_freq.xml); the
                constraint allows annual data only. A constraint attached to another dataflow is ignored. -->
